       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is about 129 mg/kg/day for a 70 kg patient. That is in the range associated with acute liver injury and is not a therapeutic dose. I don't know of any indication that calls for it, and a single 3000 mg dose repeated three times a day would likely cause serious harm.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within safe limits.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day), or up to 4,000 mg/day if your institution allows it, such as 1000 mg PO four times daily.\n- **Add a note** to the order, such as \"max 3 g/day from all sources.\"\n- **Help you reach pharmacy or your attending.** If you think this patient needs an unusual dose, they can review it and enter it through the proper channel.\n\nIf a typo or a miscommunication led to the 3000 mg figure, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
